  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $187\\,349$\n\nII. $3\\,121\\,557$\n\nIII. $99\\,125\\,041$",
  "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $187\\,349$ is\n\n$$\n1+8+7+3+4+9=32,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $187\\,349$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $3\\,121\\,557$ is\n\n$$\n3+1+2+1+5+5+7=24,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $3\\,121\\,557$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $99\\,125\\,041$ is\n\n$$\n9+9+1+2+5+0+4+1=31,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $99\\,125\\,041$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
